    "result_text": "Done. The build compiles and all tests pass, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe response DTOs are generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by MapStruct from `@Transient` getters on the `Owner` domain model \u2014 the same pattern used by `displayName`, `membershipNumber`, etc. I followed it and kept each piece of logic in its own small unit:\n\n1. **`model/CountryDialingCode.java`** (new) \u2014 extracted the country-code knowledge (code \u2192 national-digit-length: `61`\u21929, `1`\u219210) that was previously *private* inside `TelephoneNormalizer` into one shared table with `matching(...)` and `nationalLength(...)`. This is now the single source of truth for country codes.\n\n2. **`model/TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 a static formatter (matching the `Luhn`/`RegionPostcodeTable` style) that inverts E.164: splits the country code via `CountryDialingCode`, then groups the national digits in threes \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`.\n\n3. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getTelephoneDisplay()` delegating to `TelephoneDisplay.format(telephone)`. `telephone` itself is untouched and stays raw E.164.\n\n4. **`rest/controller/TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 refactored to reuse `CountryDialingCode` instead of its own private copy, so the two features share one country-code definition rather than duplicating it (behavior preserved).\n\n5. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `telephoneDisplay` as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` schema. MapStruct auto-maps it by name; no mapper or controller changes were needed.",
